   "source": [
    "**b) Compute the global mean temperature time series**\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "f5709f01-d8d4-4823-aacc-a3b5579b054d",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "**c) Plot the global mean  temperature time series from 1948-2025 with proper axis labels and units**"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 88,
   "id": "50383e89-fc5c-4a13-8c7b-1f6eeca92bd8",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "data": {
      "image/png": "",
      "text/plain": [
       "<Figure size 640x480 with 1 Axes>"
      ]
     },
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "display_data"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "\n",
    "glob_mean = Air.mean(dim = ['lat','lon'])                                            #Calculating the global mean \n",
    "glob_mean.plot()                                                                     #Plotting the global mean temperature time series\n",
    "plt.xlabel('Time')\n",
    "plt.ylabel('Air temperature (in Kelvin)')\n",
    "plt.title('Global mean temperature time series')\n",
    "plt.grid(True)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "91c8a08a-11c2-4cdc-9535-3cafc2aec89e",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "**BONUS**"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 109,
   "id": "e46979b7-f1ae-433c-a86e-c62afd41748d",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "Area weighted global mean is 177.96732\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "weight = np.cos(np.deg2rad(Lat))\n",
    "mean_weight = glob_mean*weight\n",
    "area_weighted_mean = np.mean(mean_weight)\n",
    "print('Area weighted global mean is',area_weighted_mean.values)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "d7f95e4e-bb10-4038-ac56-c3b06a0e109f",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "**d) Solution -  As we can clearly see from the above graph that the trend is showing an overall increasing trend in air temperature,with seasonally increasing and decreasing natue per year**"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "fd0b106b-73f2-44f5-ad46-23f7073d318b",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Q.2) SAMPLING VARIABILITY AND CONFIDENCE INTERVALS"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "0db57270-3cec-4074-8fff-48017866e11a",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "**a) Extract Period A and Period B from global mean time series . Compute the sample mean and standard eviation for each period**  "
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 27,
   "id": "dc5344d6-575e-4f1a-8ed1-7f542b47835c",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "The no of months in Sample A is 360\n",
      "The no of months in Sample B is 360\n",
      "The sample mean for period A is 277.62436\n",
      "The sample mean for period B is 278.55313\n",
      "The standard deviation for period A is 0.14079736173152924\n",
      "The standard deviation for period B is 0.2860044538974762\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "samp_A = glob_mean.sel(time = slice('1948-01-01','1977-12-31'))               # Extracting the Sample A (time period = 1948-1977)\n",
    "samp_B = glob_mean.sel(time = slice('1995-01-01','2024-12-31'))               # Extracting the Sample A (time period = 1995-2024) \n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"The no of months in Sample A is\",len(samp_A))                          \n",
    "print(\"The no of months in Sample B is\",len(samp_B))\n",
    "\n",
    "ann_A = samp_A.groupby('time.year').mean('time')                # Calculating the annual mean for Period A from monthly mean (from 360 to 30 time steps)\n",
    "ann_B = samp_B.groupby('time.year').mean('time')                # Calculating the annual mean for Period B from monthly mean (from 360 to 30 time steps)\n",
    "\n",
    "mean_A = np.mean(ann_A)                                         # Sample mean for period A\n",
    "mean_B = np.mean(ann_B)                                         # Sample mean for period B\n",
    "\n",
    "std_A = np.std(ann_A)                                           # Standard deviation for Sample A\n",
    "std_B = np.std(ann_B)                                           # Standard deviatiopn for Sample B\n",
    "\n",
    "print('The sample mean for period A is',mean_A.values)\n",
    "print('The sample mean for period B is',mean_B.values)\n",
    "print('The standard deviation for period A is',std_A.values)\n",
    "print('The standard deviation for period B is',std_B.values)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "8b68efb7-f924-4f72-ac64-ae41676ccbcc",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "**b) Compute the 95% confidence intervals for mean of each period using the T distribution**"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 41,
   "id": "3b0e7904-aeb2-4ce4-990f-0624d5aded43",
