  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "5391835b-a838-4eec-b4d9-a07d5cacfc2f",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "**c) In 3-4 sentences , explain**\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "**(i) What sampling variability means in climate data** \n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "**(ii) Why CI widths may differ between the two periods**\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "**(iii)How to interpret a 95% CI**"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "c6f00e8d-067d-4fe8-8313-fdededa6571b",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "**Solution -(i) Sampling variability simply means the observable change in the means and standard deviations of the climate data when the input sample is different**\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "**(ii) CI widths may differ when the confidence interval percentage considered is different , like it will vary in 95% and 99%**\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "**(iii) 95% CI interprets that out of all values we are taking into consideration , the 95% of these values will hold the true value we are looking for**"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "66cd7fc6-730a-4d17-9561-f74a08dd3cd4",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Q.3) HYPOTHESIS TESTING FOR CLIMATE CHANGE DETECTION"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "f2d56bce-014d-47ff-b6e1-632f83c6dab8",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "**a) Perform a two sample T test (equal variances allowed), Compute the T statistic,degrees of freedom,and p value . State whether the warming is significant at 5% level**"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 55,
   "id": "1e6d0184-6fb0-4d46-ab1d-ee623f0028c7",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "T statistic -15.68965013955302\n",
      "P value 1.5554099894000495e-22\n",
      "The degrees of freedom is 58\n",
      "Warming is significantly different.\n",
      "Null hypothesis is rejected\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "from scipy.stats import ttest_ind\n",
    "t_stat, p_value = ttest_ind(ann_A.values, ann_B.values)\n",
    "print('T statistic' , t_stat)\n",
    "print('P value',p_value)\n",
    "print(\"The degrees of freedom is\",(len(ann_A)+len(ann_B)-2))\n",
    "alpha = 0.05\n",
    "if p_value < alpha:                                                             # H0 = NULL HYPOTHESIS ( MuA = MuB)\n",
    "    print(\"Warming is significantly different.\")\n",
    "else:                                                                          # H1 = ALTERNATE HYPOTHESIS(MuB> MuA)\n",
    "    print(\"No significant difference in Warming.\")\n",
    "\n",
    "print('Null hypothesis is rejected')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "1ef94241-ca55-4cb8-8359-5f4b6d763860",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "**b) Perform an F test for equality of variances . Compute the F statistic using the larger sample variance in the numerator, compute with 5% critical value**"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 56,
   "id": "7e10c572-c76a-4040-a647-62f13a702487",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "Variance for sample A 0.020507479086518288\n",
      "Variance for sample B 0.0846191942691803\n",
      "F statistic 4.126260176210997\n",
      "P value 0.00013513167503768136\n",
      "The variances of the two samples are significantly different.\n",
      "Null hypothesis is rejected\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "from scipy.stats import f\n",
    "varA = np.var(ann_A,ddof=1)                                                      # Variance for sample A\n",
    "varB = np.var(ann_B,ddof=1)                                                      # Variance for sample B\n",
    "print('Variance for sample A',varA.values)\n",
    "print('Variance for sample B',varB.values)\n",
    "f_stat = varB/varA\n",
    "df1 = len(ann_A)-1                                                              # degrees of reedom for Sample A\n",
    "df2= len(ann_B)-1                                                               # degrees of freedom for Sample B\n",
    "p_value = f.sf(f_stat, df2, df1)\n",
    "print('F statistic',f_stat.values)\n",
    "print('P value' , p_value)\n",
    "alpha = 0.05\n",
    "if p_value < alpha:                                                                   # H0 = NULL HYPOTHESIS ( Var1 = Var2)\n",
    "    print(\"The variances of the two samples are significantly different.\")\n",
    "else:                                                                                 # H1 = ALTERNATE HYPOTHESIS(Var1 ~= Var2)\n",
    "    print(\"No significant difference between the two sample variances.\")\n",
    "\n",
    "print('Null hypothesis is rejected')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "321376fd-fdb0-4f48-a6d6-ba1e1219e757",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
